course: dictionary
lesson: 8990
title: Old money and tricky words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words belong to a time long ago. «Sing a song of sixpence» is a nursery rhyme, and sixpence is a word you will meet in old stories and history lessons. You may not know it, but the context can help: look for clues about money, prices and coins.
explain: «Toad bargains for six shillings and sixpence and as much stew as he can eat.» Bargains means makes a deal over a price, so sixpence is part of a price. Shillings and sixpence are both money, so sixpence must be a coin or an amount of money.
explain: Now check your guess. «Two sixpences made a shilling, and prices were much smaller then.» If two sixpences make one shilling, one sixpence is half a shilling. Your meaning fits every clue, so you can trust it.
fact: A sixpence was a small British coin worth six old pennies.
fact: Twelve pennies made a shilling, and twenty shillings made a pound, so a sixpence was half a shilling.
fact: Sixpence can also mean the amount of six old pennies, as in «sixpence» for a price.
fact: «Sing a song of sixpence» is a famous nursery rhyme.
fact: Some families still hide a silver sixpence in the Christmas pudding for luck.
exercise: How many old pennies was one sixpence worth? | Two | Twenty | *Six | Twelve
exercise: «He knocks over a fussy old rabbit who wants sixpence to let him pass.» What does the rabbit want? | A hat | A ride on a cart | *Money, a sixpence coin | A carrot
exercise: The phrase «turn on a sixpence» means what? | Sing very loudly | Pay six pennies for a pie | Fall over in a field | *Turn very quickly in a small space
test: In «Sing a song of sixpence», what is a sixpence? | *An old coin | A kind of stew | A ship | A bird
test: How many pennies made a shilling? | Ten | *Twelve | Twenty | Six
exam: Which statement about a sixpence is true? | A sixpence was worth six shillings | A sixpence was used only in Australia | *A sixpence was worth six old pennies | A sixpence is a kind of bread
